---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getUrl } from '../../utils/nav';
---

<BaseLayout title="Core POS Benchmarking" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href={getUrl('/projects')} class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>Core POS Benchmarking & Longitudinal Audit</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Established six quantitative benchmark metrics across 12 core user flows and later validated performance in a live development environment.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Retail operations</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Lead researcher</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Time on task, error frequency, ease-of-use scoring</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Establishing usability baselines and tracking performance over time</h2>
          <p>To drive continuous improvement in point-of-sale systems, we needed to establish clear performance baselines and track changes across multiple years. This required developing a rigorous audit methodology and comparative framework.</p>
          <p>The longitudinal benchmarking revealed key friction points in checkout experiences and provided data-driven justification for prioritizing improvements. This work became the foundation for product roadmap decisions and demonstrated ROI on design investments.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
